  "findings": [
    "Durable metrics favour exeris on all three axes (rps, CPU/req, RSS).",
    "Jackson-3 tax refuted: in-profile share lower than qtuned's Jackson-2, and JMH shows J3 faster at equal alloc.",
    "Exeris does the MOST syscalls/req but the LEAST kernel-CPU/req: cheaper syscalls, not fewer.",
    "On loopback, NET_RX softirq is inline in worker syscall context (captured per-PID); no ksoftirqd consumer."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Loopback kernel: no NIC/GSO/TSO/IRQ-coalescing; softirq inline. Fair across stacks; does not transfer to real network.",
